      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C79","C92","C98","C110","C120"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No query-specific oral or intravenous pharmacokinetic data exist.",
    "No direct F measurement for the query in any level.",
    "L3 exposure records are for other molecules; cinnarizine data are from dogs with cyclodextrin formulations and levomilnacipran data are from an ER formulation without an IV comparator.",
    "No query-specific first-pass metabolism, efflux, or solubility data are available.",
    "Low neutral fraction and high logP leave absorption uncertainty, but this is not affirmative evidence for F<20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Keep high: transferable human absolute-bioavailability contexts for structurally similar lipophilic tertiary amines/amides are above 20%, and L3 oral-exposure records for similar amides show measurable absorption without affirmative low-F evidence. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query PK exists."
